  "name": "user-validate",
  "description": "Puts an artifact (a spec, a plan or any document) to the user for a validation decision and returns exactly one outcome: approved, changes-requested or rejected. Runs on the configured backend, `plannotator` (browser review, opt-in) or `internal` (structured prompt, the default). Use when a workflow stage needs the user's approval, sign-off or go/no-go before it proceeds, or when the user must arbitrate between options. Also use to work out the effective gate configuration (validation.conf) or the outcome a gate run returns. Trigger terms: user gate, validation gate, gate configuration, gate outcome, approval, sign-off, approve this plan, plannotator review. Not for reviewing a pull request (pr-reviewer), writing a spec (spec-author) or annotating a file on the user's own initiative (plannotator).",
